WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.709
RUFUS: Access and confidence are, again,
different documents.

00:00:03.922 --> 00:00:06.233
JAMIE: He's going to put that on a mug.

00:00:06.298 --> 00:00:07.779
RUFUS: I've earned it today.

00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:13.236
ALEX: But here's what I find genuinely
interesting — Google choosing Oracle
specifically.

00:00:13.236 --> 00:00:18.481
ALEX: Oracle has enterprise credibility
in industries where Google Cloud
historically hasn't. Finance,

00:00:18.481 --> 00:00:23.725
ALEX: healthcare-adjacent workloads,
government-adjacent procurement.

00:00:23.835 --> 00:00:27.732
RUFUS: That's the non-obvious part of
the channel strategy. It's not just
distribution.

00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:31.628
RUFUS: It's credibility transfer.
Oracle's existing relationships carry
Google's chips into rooms where

00:00:31.628 --> 00:00:35.525
RUFUS: Google wouldn't have been the
first call.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:40.094
JAMIE: Which means TPU adoption might
happen sideways — not because a
developer

00:00:40.094 --> 00:00:44.552
JAMIE: chose them, but because a
procurement team already trusted Oracle.
